since moongeun became president the  South Korean government has cracked down  on North Korean defectors raising  awareness of the horrors they endured  under the Kim regime North Korea is  responsible for the death of millions by  starvation it has imprisoned tens of  thousands and political gulags and Kim  jong-un arguably runs the cruelest  tyranny in the world it's no wonder that  each year more than 1,000 North Koreans  risk their lives to escape but instead  of praising defectors for highlighting  these abuses the democratically elected  moon government has chosen to silence  them as part of its policy of reproach  Minh TWiT the North moons government has  repeatedly asked defectors to stop  criticizing North Korea as it did during  the 2018 Olympics but it doesn't stop  there  it has allegedly used security services  to spy on defectors denied their human  rights group to access to government  support proposed textbook edits that  minimize North Korea's military  provocations and prevented defectors  from sending information pamphlets about  South Korea across the border the goal  of bringing peace to the Korean  Peninsula is a noble one but  prioritizing unification over human  freedom is not the answer  do you think South Korea should do more  to support North Korean defectors let us  know in our poll also let us know what  other topics you'd like to see our  scholars cover in 60 seconds and be sure  to LIKE and subscribe for more research  and videos from AEI
 

